{title: Reason to Dance}
{artist: Jonathan Stockstill, Corey Bastin, Dustin West}
{key: Em}
{tempo: 127}

{comment: Intro}
[C] [G] [D] [Am7]

{comment: Verse 1}
[Em]What has He done for [G]you?
Has He [D]given life, Has He [Am7]given freedom
[Em]What has He done for [G]you?
Has He [D]given hope, Has He [Am7]given healing

{comment: Pre-Chorus}
[Em]Yes He has for [G]me  - - [D]He's done it [Am7]for me.
[Em]Yes He has for [G]you.      [D]
So if you're feeling alive, then sing it out.

{comment: Chorus}
[C]We won't let the [G]rocks cry out [D]instead of us,
[Am7]We will lift our [C]voices, [G]voices to [D]you.
[C]We will tell the [G]world of all He’s done for [D]us,
[Am7]We will lift our [C]voices, [G]voices to [D]you.
You've given us a reason to [C]dance!   [G]     [D]    [Am7]

{comment: Bridge}
[Em]
